      "message": "[Major] Calling `xa_load` on `mapping-\u003ei_pages` without holding the RCU read lock (`rcu_read_lock()`) can lead to a use-after-free of XArray nodes if the page cache is concurrently modified (e.g., via truncation). Furthermore, because the folios returned by `xa_load` are not pinned or locked, they can be concurrently freed and reused. Calling `set_bit` on a freed/reused folio\u0027s flags can corrupt page states of other active kernel allocations, leading to kernel instability or potential privilege escalation.\n\nNote: You can bypass this security scan by adding \u0027SECURITY_PRESUBMIT_BYPASS_REASON\u003dyour_reason\u0027 in your commit message.\nFor more details or to provide feedback, visit go/warden-presubmit.",
